      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Data Interoperability Digital Business Capability refers to the ability of an organization to seamlessly exchange and integrate data across various systems, applications, and platforms. It involves the establishment of standardized data formats, protocols, and interfaces to enable efficient and effective data sharing and collaboration.&#xA;&#xA;This capability encompasses the ability to overcome the challenges associated with data heterogeneity, inconsistency, and incompatibility. It involves the development and implementation of data integration strategies, technologies, and frameworks to ensure that data can be easily understood, accessed, and utilized by different systems and stakeholders.&#xA;&#xA;The Data Interoperability Digital Business Capability involves several key components and activities:&#xA;&#xA;1. Data Integration: This involves the consolidation and integration of data from disparate sources, such as databases, applications, and external systems. It includes the extraction, transformation, and loading (ETL) processes to ensure that data is cleansed, standardized, and made compatible with the target systems.&#xA;&#xA;2. Data Mapping and Transformation: This component focuses on defining and implementing mappings between different data formats, structures, and schemas. It involves the conversion of data from one format to another, ensuring that data can be effectively exchanged and understood by different systems.&#xA;&#xA;3. Data Governance: This aspect involves the establishment of policies, standards, and guidelines for data management and interoperability. It includes defining data quality requirements, data ownership, and data security measures to ensure that data is accurate, reliable, and protected during its exchange and integration.&#xA;&#xA;4. Data Exchange Protocols and Standards: This component involves the adoption and implementation of industry-standard protocols and formats for data exchange. Examples include XML, JSON, RESTful APIs, and web services. These standards enable seamless communication and interoperability between different systems and platforms.&#xA;&#xA;5. Data Security and Privacy: This capability also encompasses ensuring the security and privacy of data during its exchange and integration. It involves implementing encryption, access controls, and data anonymization techniques to protect sensitive information and comply with relevant regulations and policies.&#xA;&#xA;6. Data Analytics and Insights: This component focuses on leveraging the integrated data to derive meaningful insights and support data-driven decision-making. It involves the use of data analytics tools and techniques to extract valuable information, identify patterns, and uncover trends from the integrated data.&#xA;&#xA;Overall, the Data Interoperability Digital Business Capability plays a crucial role in enabling organizations to leverage the full potential of their data assets. It facilitates seamless data exchange, integration, and collaboration, leading to improved operational efficiency, enhanced decision-making, and the ability to quickly respond to changing business needs."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="EIRA Team"/>
      <property key="dct:source"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Data Spaces [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Data Spaces"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Organisational view"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalBusinessCapability"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Diagnosis" id="id-e5c4ec9fb863401a8d8e6c84a64899a4">
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The capability to digitally support medical diagnosis and tele-diagnosis. It aims at determining the nature of a cause of a disease or of a situation / condition and at assessing / monitoring the health status of a patient (i.e. personal health status, factors that influence health)."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Health Organisational view [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Digital Business Capabilities Catalogue"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="health"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DiagnosisCapability"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalBusinessCapability"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Provision of specialist and nursing cares" id="id-eb78fcb760c14f3f97ee01173b48c05d">
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The capability to digitally support the provision of specialist and nursing cares. Specialist and nursing care is composed of two different types of provisions:  Outpatient health care (medical procedures, tests, and services that can be provided to the patient in a setting that doesn't involve an overnight hospital stay) and Inpatient health care (medical treatment administered to a patient whose condition requires treatment in a hospital or other health care facility)."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Health Organisational view [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Digital Business Capabilities Catalogue"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="health"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ProvisionOfSpecialistAndNursingCaresCapability"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalBusinessCapability"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Population investigation and diagnosis" id="id-ec19a2c955ab4b178c09342ae8bb8e51">
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The capability to digitally support investigations and diagnosis to identify and address health problems and hazards affecting or that could affect the population."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Health Organisational view [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Digital Business Capabilities Catalogue"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="health"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/PopulationInvestigationAndDiagnosisCapability"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalBusinessCapability"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Resource allocation" id="id-ed3ae69ffbfa41d990db23d426dd3afd">
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The capability to digitally support healthcare resource budget allocation and monitoring. It also includes the remuneration management (setting remuneration methods for health workers), the healthcare facility management funding and the medical equipment renovation/maintenance funding."/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Health Organisational view [Motivation]"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="OV-Digital Business Capabilities Catalogue"/>
      <property key="eira:businessDomain" value="health"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Organisational"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/ResourceAllocationCapability"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DigitalBusinessCapability"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Capability" name="Data Lineage" id="id-ed8a2438043941e58c6136f42f6ef07d">
      <documentation>Description: The Data Lineage Digital Business Capability refers to the ability of an organization to track and trace the origin, movement, and transformation of data throughout its lifecycle. It involves capturing and documenting the lineage of data elements, including their sources, transformations, and destinations. This capability enables organizations to understand the data flow across systems, processes, and applications, ensuring data quality, compliance, and effective decision-making. It also helps in identifying data dependencies, impact analysis, and troubleshooting data-related issues. Overall, the Data Lineage Digital Business Capability provides transparency and visibility into the data ecosystem, facilitating effective data governance and management.

Additional information: The Data Lineage Digital Business Capability refers to the ability of an organization to track and trace the origin, movement, and transformation of data throughout its lifecycle. It involves capturing and documenting the lineage of data elements, including their sources, transformations, and destinations, to ensure data quality, compliance, and understanding.

Data lineage provides a comprehensive view of how data flows through various systems, processes, and applications within an organization. It helps in understanding the data's journey, identifying potential bottlenecks, and ensuring data integrity and accuracy. This capability enables organizations to answer critical questions about data, such as where it comes from, how it is transformed, and where it goes.

The Data Lineage Digital Business Capability encompasses several key components and activities:

1. Data Source Identification: This involves identifying the original sources of data, whether it is internal or external to the organization. It includes understanding the systems, databases, files, or APIs that generate or provide data.

2. Data Transformation Mapping: This component focuses on documenting the transformations applied to data as it moves through different processes, systems, or applications. It includes capturing the rules, algorithms, or logic used to modify or manipulate the data.

3. Data Destination Tracking: This aspect involves tracking the final destinations of data, such as databases, reports, dashboards, or other systems. It ensures that data reaches the intended targets and helps in identifying any potential gaps or inconsistencies.

4. Metadata Management: Metadata, which provides additional context and information about data, plays a crucial role in data lineage. This component involves managing and maintaining metadata repositories, including data dictionaries, data catalogs, and data models.

5. Data Lineage Visualization: Visualizing data lineage helps stakeholders understand the flow of data across systems and processes. It may include graphical representations, diagrams, or interactive tools that depict the relationships and dependencies between data elements.

6. Impact Analysis: Data lineage enables impact analysis by identifying the potential consequences of changes to data sources, transformations, or destinations. It helps in assessing the impact on downstream systems, processes, and reports, facilitating effective change management.

7. Compliance and Audit: Data lineage is essential for regulatory compliance and audit purposes. It enables organizations to demonstrate data lineage to regulatory bodies, ensuring data governance, privacy, and security requirements are met.

8. Data Quality Monitoring: Data lineage supports data quality initiatives by providing insights into the data's journey and identifying potential quality issues. It helps in establishing data quality metrics, monitoring data quality, and implementing corrective actions.

Overall, the Data Lineage Digital Business Capability is a critical aspect of data management and governance. It enables organizations to have a holistic view of their data assets, understand data flows, ensure data integrity, comply with regulations, and make informed decisions based on trustworthy and reliable data.

Example: The Data Lineage Digital Business Capability in the public sector refers to the ability to track and understand the origin, movement, and transformation of data throughout its lifecycle. This capability is crucial for ensuring data quality, compliance, and decision-making. Here are some real examples of how this capability is applied in the public sector:

1. Tax Compliance: In tax administration, data lineage is used to trace the flow of financial data from taxpayers' records to tax returns and subsequent reports. This capability helps auditors and tax authorities verify the accuracy and integrity of the data, ensuring compliance with tax regulations.

2. Fraud Detection: Government agencies responsible for detecting and preventing fraud, such as social welfare fraud or tax evasion, utilize data lineage to track the flow of data across various systems and processes. By analyzing the lineage, anomalies or suspicious patterns can be identified, leading to the detection of fraudulent activities.

3. Public Health Monitoring: Data lineage is crucial in public health monitoring, especially during disease outbreaks or pandemics. It helps track the origin and movement of patient data, test results, and contact tracing information. This capability enables health authorities to identify the source of infection, track the spread of the disease, and make informed decisions for containment and mitigation.

4. Government Performance Reporting: Data lineage is used to ensure the accuracy and reliability of performance reports generated by government agencies. By tracing the data sources, transformations, and calculations involved in generating these reports, data lineage helps maintain transparency, accountability, and trust in the reported performance metrics.

5. Freedom of Information Requests: Public sector organizations often receive requests for information under the Freedom of Information Act or similar legislation. Data lineage helps track the data sources, systems, and processes involved in generating the requested information. This capability ensures that the information provided is accurate, complete, and can be audited if necessary.

These examples demonstrate how the Data Lineage Digital Business Capability is applied in the public sector to ensure data quality, compliance, and informed decision-making.

Publisher: EIRA Team

LOST view: OV-Data Spaces [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataLineageCapability

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalBusinessCapability

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-07-11

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DataLineageCapability

dct:title: Data Lineage Digital Business Capability

</documentation>
