    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Interoperability Policy" id="id-9fcbe58d197b40cfb51b68f79fbf8840">
      <documentation>Definition: An Interoperability Policy is a set of guidelines that outlines how different systems and data should work together seamlessly within an organization or across entities. It ensures that data formats, protocols, and interfaces are compatible and consistent, enabling effective data sharing and collaboration. The policy promotes the use of open standards and best practices to facilitate smooth communication and integration between various systems, applications, and stakeholders.

Source: EIF

Source reference: https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/InteroperabilityPolicyBusinessObject

ABB name: egovera:InteroperabilityPolicyBusinessObject

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/InteroperabilityPolicyBusinessObject

Interoperability Layer: Semantic

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataPolicy

</documentation>
