    <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Blockchain policy" id="id-a69129196eed4edaaa68cc691de36500">
      <documentation>Definition: A Blockchain policy, as a specialization of a Data policy, can be defined as a set of rules, guidelines, and controls that govern the management, access, and utilization of data within a blockchain network or ecosystem. It outlines the specific protocols, procedures, and requirements for storing, validating, and securing data on the blockchain, ensuring integrity, immutability, and transparency.

Source: OECD

Source reference: https://www.oecd.org/daf/blockchain/

LOST view: SV-Governance Architecture Principles

