    <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="Turtle" id="id-a63783da5ef64b8e92a45932b5bf9c5d">
      <documentation>Description: Turtle (Terse RDF Triple Language) is a human-readable serialization format for representing RDF (Resource Description Framework) data. It provides a concise and compact syntax to express triples, which consist of subject-predicate-object statements. Turtle is widely used for creating and sharing RDF data due to its simplicity and readability.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/turtle/

LOST view: SV-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TurtleRepresentation

