    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="eNotification" id="id-4ef4dd2dba2540cf9be47e1b8bf360a6">
      <documentation>Definition: The eNotification Application service refers to a software application or component that enables the electronic delivery of notifications, alerts, and messages to individuals or organizations. It operates at the application layer in a software architecture, providing the necessary functionality to create, manage, and distribute notifications through various channels

Source: International Journal of Engineering Research &amp; Technology

Source reference: https://www.ijert.org/research/managing-user-notifications-in-enterprise-applications-IJERTV7IS010324.pdf

LOST view: TVA-API Enablers [Motivation]

