    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Multimedia distribution" id="id-05b743d03ff94acdaa7645f952ff9792">
      <documentation>Definition: Multimedia Distribution refers to a data management application service that facilitates the efficient and scalable distribution of multimedia content, such as audio, video, images, and other multimedia formats. It encompasses the storage, retrieval, and delivery of multimedia assets to end-users or target systems. This service typically involves the use of network infrastructure, content delivery networks (CDNs), and streaming technologies to ensure fast and reliable delivery of multimedia content across various devices and platforms. Multimedia Distribution services play a crucial role in enabling widespread access to multimedia content, supporting entertainment, education, communication, and other domains.

Source: International Telecommunication Union (ITU)

LOST view: TVA-Functional Architecture Principles

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/MultimediaDistributionApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:MultimediaDistributionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/MultimediaDistributionApplicationService

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/DataManagementApplicationService

</documentation>
