    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Digital Certification eSignature Service" id="id-0f788d4ebd874647a39e635dc75cf770">
      <documentation>Definition: The Digital Certification eSignature Service enables users to securely sign electronic documents using digital certificates. It leverages cryptographic techniques to ensure the integrity, authenticity, and non-repudiation of digitally signed documents. This service provides a user-friendly interface accessible via the web, allowing users to upload their documents, apply their digital signature, and generate a digitally signed version. It utilizes digital certificate authorities to issue and manage digital certificates, providing a trusted framework for electronic signatures. The Digital Certification eSignature Service enhances document security, eliminates the need for physical signatures, and supports the digital transformation of business processes.

Source: ETSI

Source reference: https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf

Interoperability Dimension: Structural IoP

LOST view: TVA-Trust Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DigitalCertificationESignatureServiceApplicationService

ABB name: egovera:DigitalCertificationESignatureServiceApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-11-20

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/DigitalCertificationESignatureServiceApplicationService

Interoperability Layer: TechnicalApplication

Specialises: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/E-SignatureVerificationAndValidationApplicationService

</documentation>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="The Digital Certification eSignature Service enables users to securely sign electronic documents using digital certificates. It leverages cryptographic techniques to ensure the integrity, authenticity, and non-repudiation of digitally signed documents. This service provides a user-friendly interface accessible via the web, allowing users to upload their documents, apply their digital signature, and generate a digitally signed version. It utilizes digital certificate authorities to issue and manage digital certificates, providing a trusted framework for electronic signatures. The Digital Certification eSignature Service enhances document security, eliminates the need for physical signatures, and supports the digital transformation of business processes."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="ETSI"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference" value="https://www.etsi.org/deliver/etsi_ts/102700_102799/10277801/01.01.01_60/ts_10277801v010101p.pdf"/>
