      <property key="skos:note" value="Red Hat OpenShift simplifies the process of developing, deploying, and scaling applications by providing a comprehensive platform that abstracts away the underlying infrastructure complexities. It offers a self-service environment for developers to easily create and deploy applications using containers, which encapsulate the application and its dependencies. OpenShift provides features like automated scaling, load balancing, and continuous integration/continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipelines, enabling teams to rapidly iterate and deliver software. It also offers built-in security features, such as role-based access control (RBAC) and image scanning, to ensure the integrity and compliance of applications. With its support for multiple cloud providers and on-premises environments, OpenShift offers flexibility and portability for applications across different infrastructures."/>
