      <property key="skos:note" value="In a centralized identity management system, all user identities and access privileges are stored and managed in a central repository. This allows organizations to streamline user provisioning, authentication, and authorization processes, ensuring consistent and secure access to resources across various applications and systems. Centralized identity management enables administrators to efficiently manage user accounts, assign roles and permissions, and enforce security policies from a single point of control. It also simplifies user onboarding and offboarding processes, enhances security by enforcing strong authentication measures, and provides auditing and reporting capabilities for compliance purposes."/>
