    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Patient summary system" id="id-2dd56601e716461ab4701cad727a1830">
      <documentation>Definition: The use or consumption of features provided by a Patient summary system enabling the management of patient summaries base registry at national level.

Source: HealthIT.gov

Source reference: https://www.healthit.gov/topic/health-it-basics/patient-summary

Additional information: The Patient Summary System is a crucial tool in modern healthcare, enabling seamless communication between different healthcare providers and ensuring that all relevant information is available when needed. It can include a wide range of data, from basic demographic information to detailed medical histories. The system is typically designed to be easily accessible and user-friendly, allowing healthcare providers to quickly find the information they need. It can also include features such as alerts for potential drug interactions or allergies. By providing a comprehensive overview of a patient's health, the Patient Summary System can help healthcare providers make more informed decisions and provide better care.

Example: A doctor in an emergency department can quickly access a patient's summary to understand their medical history and current medications, helping them make urgent treatment decisions.

A specialist can use the Patient Summary System to review a referred patient's previous treatments and tests, reducing the need for duplicate procedures.

A pharmacist can check a patient's summary for potential drug interactions or allergies before dispensing medication.

LOST view: TVA-Health Patient Summary Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/PatientSummarySystemApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

