    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="EHDS2 Node" id="id-487ff82891084f69b4f2b08b1dc0601a">
      <documentation>Description: EHDS2 Node is a digital service that provides a platform for data sharing and communication between different systems in a network. It is designed to facilitate interoperability, data exchange, and seamless communication in a secure and efficient manner.

Additional information: EHDS2 Node is a crucial component in a network that serves as a connection point, can receive, create, store or send data along distributed network routes. Each node requires a unique identifier, which can be its own independent address or be referenced relative to other nodes. Nodes can also have multiple data points, such as IP addresses, which can be used to access additional node information. EHDS2 Node is particularly useful in complex network architectures, including blockchain networks, distributed databases, and telecommunication networks. It ensures secure data transmission and enhances the overall efficiency of the network.

Example: 1. In a healthcare setting, EHDS2 Node can be used to share patient data between different healthcare providers, ensuring seamless coordination and improved patient care. 2. In a blockchain network, EHDS2 Node can be used to validate and relay transactions, contributing to the decentralization and security of the network. 3. In a telecommunication network, EHDS2 Node can facilitate the transmission and routing of data, ensuring efficient communication.

Publisher: European Health Data Space

Source: https://health.ec.europa.eu/ehealth-digital-health-and-care/european-health-data-space_en

LOST view: TVA-Health Data Space Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EHDS2NodeApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Last modification: 2023-08-04

dct:identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/EHDS2NodeApplicationService

dct:title: EHDS2 Node Application Service

</documentation>
