    <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationService" name="Telemetry Monitoring System (TMS)" id="id-5bfb08249b2146db914ae668a2b4ab13">
      <documentation>Definition: The use or consumption of feature provided by a Telemetry Monitoring System (TMS). It refers to a Service/System enabling the autonomous remotely monitoring of patients health parameters.

Source: Techopedia

Source reference: https://www.techopedia.com/definition/14358/telemetry

Additional information: A Telemetry Monitoring System (TMS) is a sophisticated technology that enables the remote monitoring and collection of information from various sources. This system is designed to automatically collect data from different objects, compile it, and transmit it to an IT system in a different location. The data can be anything from performance metrics of a machine in a factory, vital signs of a patient in a hospital, to the speed and fuel consumption of a vehicle. The main advantage of a TMS is that it allows for real-time monitoring and immediate response to any changes or anomalies, which can be critical in industries where timely and accurate data is crucial. It also reduces the need for manual data collection and the associated risks of errors or delays.

Example: 1. In healthcare, a TMS can be used to monitor patients' vital signs and alert medical staff if any abnormalities are detected. This can be particularly useful in intensive care units or for patients with chronic conditions.
2. In manufacturing, a TMS can be used to monitor the performance of machinery and equipment. This can help to identify any potential issues or breakdowns before they occur, reducing downtime and maintenance costs.
3. In aerospace, a TMS can be used to collect and transmit data from aircraft or spacecraft, providing valuable information about their condition and performance.

LOST view: TVA-Health Patient Summary Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/TelemetryMonitoringSystemApplicationService

EIRA traceability: eira:DigitalSolutionApplicationService

