    <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="W3C Shapes Constraint Language" id="id-6004e21cc8c04bfda77e2d8c27948ffe">
      <documentation>Description: The Shapes Constraint Language (SHACL) is a language and framework for describing and validating the structure and constraints of RDF (Resource Description Framework) graphs. RDF is a standard for representing data in a graph format, widely used in the Semantic Web.

Publisher: W3C

Source: https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl/

LOST view: SV-Agnostic Ontologies

