    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Interoperable Europe Act " id="id-8a220eb7b34c4e7cafa1d764dc739389">
      <documentation>Description: The Interoperable Europe Act is a proposal for a regulation that aims to establish a high level of public sector interoperability across the European Union. The regulation seeks to promote the seamless exchange of data and information between public sector entities, including national, regional, and local authorities, as well as public service providers. The proposal outlines a framework for achieving interoperability, including the development of common standards, the use of open data, and the establishment of a European Interoperability Framework. The regulation also includes provisions for ensuring data protection and privacy, as well as measures to promote transparency and accountability in the use of public sector data. Overall, the Interoperable Europe Act aims to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of public services across the EU by facilitating the exchange of information and data between different public sector entities.

Publisher: EUR-Lex

Source: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A52022PC0720

Last modification: 26/06/2023

EIRA traceability: eira:BindingInstrumentRequirement

LOST view: Legal view - Binding Power and Jurisdiction

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Additional identifier: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=CELEX%3A52022PC0720

Title: Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL laying down measures for a high level of public sector interoperability across the Union (Interoperable Europe Act)

Example: The Interoperable Europe Act aims to improve the interoperability of public sector services across the European Union. Here are some examples of how this regulation could be applied:

</documentation>
