Title: Regulation (EU) 2022/868 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30 May 2022 on European data governance and amending Regulation (EU) 2018/1724 (Data Governance Act) (Text with EEA relevance)

</documentation>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/868/oj"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Regulation (EU) 2022/868 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30 May 2022 on European data governance and amending Regulation (EU) 2018/1724 (Data Governance Act) (Text with EEA relevance)"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="The Data Governance Act is a regulation enacted by the European Parliament and Council that aims to establish a framework for the governance of data in the European Union. It seeks to facilitate the sharing of data across sectors and borders while ensuring the protection of individuals' rights and promoting fair competition. The act introduces rules for data intermediaries and data-sharing service providers, promoting transparency, accountability, and trust in data sharing. It also includes provisions for the creation of data spaces and the development of codes of conduct for data sharing. Additionally, the act amends the existing Regulation (EU) 2018/1724 to align it with the new data governance framework."/>
      <property key="dct:publisher" value="EUR-Lex"/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/868/oj"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Architecture Principles"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Binding Power and Jurisdiction"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Legal"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/BindingInstrumentRequirement"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Declaration for the Future of Internet" id="id-f2c77ddcbb1a4a088e2c702425ee238b">
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:SolutionBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2024-01-17"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="A Declaration for the Future of the Internet"/>
      <property key="dct:description" value="'A Declaration for the Future of the Internet' is a document that outlines the principles and values that should guide the development and use of the internet in the years to come. It emphasizes the importance of an open, accessible, and inclusive internet that respects and protects users' rights, promotes innovation, and fosters collaboration among stakeholders. The declaration calls for the protection of privacy, freedom of expression, and digital rights, while also addressing issues such as cybersecurity, digital literacy, and the ethical use of emerging technologies. It aims to provide a framework for shaping the future of the internet in a way that benefits individuals, societies, and the global community as a whole."/>
      <property key="dct:source" value="https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/library/declaration-future-internet"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="https://digital-strategy.ec.europa.eu/en/library/declaration-future-internet"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Architecture Principles"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="LV-Binding Power and Jurisdiction"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Legal"/>
      <property key="eira:implementedBy" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/Non-bindingInstrumentRequirement"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Directive 2000/31/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 8 June 2000" id="id-f6f9b471d6ca40dbaf51179b562944f1">
      <documentation>Description: Directive 2000/31/EC, known also as the Electronic Commerce Directive, is a legislation enacted by the European Parliament and Council on June 8, 2000. It focuses on the legal aspects of information society services, specifically electronic commerce, within the Internal Market of the European Union. The directive aims to establish a harmonized legal framework for online businesses, ensuring the free movement of electronic services and promoting consumer confidence in online transactions. It covers various aspects such as electronic contracts, liability of intermediaries, and rules for online advertising and commercial communications.

Publisher: EUR-Lex

Source: http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/31/oj

Last modification: 26/06/2023

EIRA traceability: eira:BindingInstrumentRequirement

LOST view: Legal view - Binding Power and Jurisdiction

EIRA concept: eira:SolutionBuildingBlock

Additional identifier: http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/31/oj

Title: Directive 2000/31/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 8 June 2000 on certain legal aspects of information society services, in particular electronic commerce, in the Internal Market ('Directive on electronic commerce')

Example: The Electronic Commerce Directive (ECD) is a European Union directive that provides legal guidelines for electronic commerce activities within the EU. Here are some examples of its application:

</documentation>
