    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions" id="id-1116059b8bab4003b43528da15498eee">
      <documentation>Definition: Health Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (HTIAS) is a grouping that covers a range of technical solutions designed to facilitate interoperability in the health sector. These solutions are particularly focused on ensuring seamless cross-border health data exchange, as exemplified by the eHealth DSI technical framework.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Health Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (HTIAS) encompasses various elements that aim to enhance the interoperability in the health sector. One such element is the eHealth DSI technical framework, which is a contract designed to facilitate cross-border health data exchange. This framework is part of the broader efforts to ensure that health data can be shared and accessed across different health systems and geographical locations, thereby improving patient care and health outcomes.

Example: An example of application of the Health Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions is the eHealth DSI technical framework. This framework is used in cross-border health data exchange, allowing health professionals in one country to access and use health data from another country. This can be particularly useful in situations where a patient from one country seeks medical treatment in another country, as it allows the health professionals in the treating country to access the patient's health data and provide appropriate care.

LOST view: TVA-Health Technical Agreements

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HealthTechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping

