      <property key="eira:PURI" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:modified" value="2023-11-20"/>
      <property key="dct:identifier" value="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="dct:title" value="Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions Catalogue"/>
      <property key="dct:type" value="egovera:BusinessAgnosticOntologiesCatalogueSolutionsGrouping"/>
      <property key="skos:definition" value="Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions (ABB) is a grouping that covers a range of ontology resources and tools that are applicable across various business domains. The catalogue includes Linked Open Vocabularies (LOV) and Ontology Design Patterns (ODP), both of which are instrumental in ontology engineering and semantic web portal design respectively."/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSource" value="EIRA Team Research"/>
      <property key="eira:definitionSourceReference"/>
      <property key="skos:example" value="For instance, a healthcare organization can use the LOV tool from the Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions to create a medical ontology linking various medical terms and concepts. Similarly, an e-commerce business can use the ODP resources to design a product ontology for their semantic web portal, linking various product categories and attributes."/>
      <property key="skos:note" value="The Business Agnostic Ontologies Catalogue Solutions (ABB) is a comprehensive collection of ontology resources that are not specific to any business domain, hence the term 'agnostic'. It includes Linked Open Vocabularies (LOV), a tool used by Ontology Engineers for creating, managing and utilizing ontologies. LOV provides a wide range of vocabularies that can be linked and utilized in various contexts. Another key component of the catalogue is OntologyDesignPatterns.org (ODP), a dedicated portal for ontology design patterns. ODP provides resources and tools for designing and implementing ontologies in a semantic web context. Both LOV and ODP are crucial for ontology engineering and semantic web design, making the catalogue a valuable resource for businesses operating in diverse domains."/>
      <property key="eira:concept" value="eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="SV-Agnostic Ontology Catalogue"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="SV-Functional Architecture Principles"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Semantic view - Motivation"/>
      <property key="eira:view" value="Semantic view"/>
      <property key="eira:eifLayer" value="Semantic"/>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions" id="id-3c675bbce13e4fb383252659380e52b3">
      <documentation>Description: Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (ABB) is a grouping that refers to actual solutions that facilitate the design, development, documentation, and consumption of APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) across different systems and platforms. These solutions are built upon various specifications and protocols such as OpenAPI, RESTful API, GraphQL, gRPC, JSON-RPC, SOAP, and OData, which provide a standard, language-agnostic interface for APIs, enabling interoperability between different systems.

Additional information: The Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions (ABB) is a comprehensive suite of solutions that leverage various API specifications and protocols to ensure seamless interaction between different systems and platforms. These solutions are built upon OpenAPI, RESTful API, GraphQL, gRPC, JSON-RPC, SOAP, and OData specifications, each offering unique features and capabilities. OpenAPI is used for designing, building, documenting, and consuming REST APIs. RESTful API is a set of rules for building web services, while GraphQL is a data query and manipulation language for APIs. gRPC is a high-performance framework for service communication, JSON-RPC is a protocol for data exchange, SOAP is a messaging protocol for program communication over the internet, and OData is a protocol for building and consuming RESTful APIs.

Example: Examples of application for the Business Agnostic API Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions include designing and building APIs for a multi-language system using OpenAPI and gRPC, creating web services using RESTful API, querying and manipulating data using GraphQL, exchanging data between a client and a server using JSON-RPC, communicating between programs running on different operating systems using SOAP, and building and consuming RESTful APIs using OData.

Publisher: EIRA Team Research

LOST view: TV-Technical Agreements

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/BusinessAgnosticAPITechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping

