    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health Medical Imaging Enablers" id="id-624c4fc56fb84cf99ac5731ccad2f81c">
      <documentation>Definition: Health Medical Imaging Enablers ABB is a Grouping that covers a range of application services designed to facilitate and enhance the process of medical imaging. These services include systems for radiology information, picture archiving and communication, audit trail and node authentication for radiology, and teaching file and clinical trial export.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Health Medical Imaging Enablers ABB encompasses various systems that play crucial roles in the medical imaging process. The Radiology Information System (RIS) Application Service is a networked software system for managing medical imagery and associated data. The Picture Archive and Communication System (PACS) Application Service is a medical imaging technology which provides economical storage and convenient access to images from multiple modalities. The Audit Trail and Node Authentication - Radiology Option System Application Service provides a secure and traceable method of accessing and managing radiology data. The Teaching File and Clinical Trial Export System (TCE) Application Service is a system that allows for the export of teaching files and clinical trial data for further study and analysis.

Example: For instance, a hospital might use the Radiology Information System (RIS) to manage patient data and scheduling, the Picture Archive and Communication System (PACS) to store and access medical images, the Audit Trail and Node Authentication - Radiology Option system to ensure secure and traceable access to radiology data, and the Teaching File and Clinical Trial Export system (TCE) to export data for teaching or clinical trials.

LOST view: TVA-Health Medical Imaging Enablers [Motivation]

