    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health Laboratory Enablers" id="id-9389312c546e4edd8040892f0a90ea96">
      <documentation>Definition: Health Laboratory Enablers ABB is a Grouping that covers a range of application services that facilitate the operation of health laboratories. These services include Laboratory Information System (LIS), Laboratory Device Automation System (LDAS), and Laboratory Barcode Labelling System (LBLS).

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Health Laboratory Enablers ABB is a collection of application services that are essential for the efficient and effective functioning of health laboratories. The Laboratory Information System (LIS) is a software that manages and stores data from all stages of medical processes and tests. The Laboratory Device Automation System (LDAS) is a system that automates the operation of laboratory devices, reducing the need for manual intervention and increasing efficiency. The Laboratory Barcode Labelling System (LBLS) is a system that uses barcodes to label and track laboratory samples, ensuring accurate identification and tracking of samples.

Example: Examples of application of these elements include a hospital laboratory using the LIS to manage patient test data, a research lab utilizing the LDAS to automate complex testing procedures, and a diagnostic lab using the LBLS to accurately track and manage samples.

LOST view: TVA-Health Laboratory Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HealthLaboratoryEnablersGrouping

