    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health Data Lake Infrastructure Enablers" id="id-b68bae7b18b84d2bbbadf3a9376fb47d">
      <documentation>Definition: Health Data Lake Infrastructure Enablers ABB is a Grouping that covers the essential components required to establish a health data lake infrastructure. These components are designed to collect, store, and manage health-related data, particularly patient vital signs data, in a secure and efficient manner. The purpose of these elements is to enable real-time monitoring of patient health and facilitate data-driven decision making in healthcare.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Health Data Lake Infrastructure Enablers ABB includes elements like 'Patient vital signs data lake'. This specific element is a data set that contains all the real-time data coming from wearable IoT devices used to monitor patient vital signs. The data lake infrastructure enables the collection and storage of large volumes of health data in its native format until it's needed. This data can then be used for various purposes such as predictive analytics, patient health monitoring, and research. The infrastructure is designed to handle the complexity and volume of data, ensuring its availability and accessibility for healthcare providers.

Example: An example of application of the Health Data Lake Infrastructure Enablers ABB is in a hospital setting where wearable IoT devices are used to monitor patient vital signs. The data from these devices is collected in real-time and stored in the 'Patient vital signs data lake'. This data can then be accessed and analyzed by healthcare professionals to monitor patient health, detect anomalies, and make informed decisions about patient care.

LOST view: TVI-Data Management and Knowledge Discovery Infrastructure Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HealthDataLakeInfrastructureEnablersGrouping

