    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health Data Representatons" id="id-d821dcddeb0d495a9722dd6e5820614d">
      <documentation>Definition: Health Data Representations is a grouping that covers various formats and specifications used to standardize and structure health-related data. This includes laboratory data formats, eHDSI data formats, FHIR specifications, and national medical data formats.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: Health Data Representations are crucial for the interoperability and exchange of health data across different systems and platforms. They ensure that health data is consistently structured and can be accurately interpreted by various health information systems. The 'Laboratory data format' is used to standardize the representation of laboratory results. The 'eHDSI (eHealth Digital Service Infrastructure) data format' is a European standard for health data exchange. The 'FHIR (Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources) Specification' is a standard for exchanging healthcare information electronically. The 'National medical data format' refers to the specific standards set by a country for structuring health data.

Example: Used in a hospital laboratory to standardize the reporting of test results.
Used in a European health information exchange project to ensure consistent data structure across participating countries.
Used in a health IT system to enable interoperability with other systems using the same standard.
Used in a national health database to ensure all data entries follow the same format.

LOST view: Semantic view

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HealthDataRepresentatonsGrouping

