    <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Health eDispensation Data Exchange Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions" id="id-f663abc8237d4f8aa9c51377c9ce74b0">
      <documentation>Definition: Health eDispensation Data Exchange Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions ABB is a grouping that covers the technical and contractual aspects of electronic prescription and pharmacy dispense data exchange. It includes elements such as SCRIPT - ePrescription exchange and IHE DIS: Pharmacy Dispense, which are contracts that govern the exchange of ePrescription and pharmacy dispense data respectively.

Source: EIRA Team Research

Additional information: The Health eDispensation Data Exchange Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions ABB is a comprehensive catalogue of elements that are integral to the technical interoperability of health data exchange systems. It includes elements like SCRIPT - ePrescription exchange, which is a contract that outlines the terms and conditions for the exchange of electronic prescriptions between healthcare providers. Another element is the IHE DIS: Pharmacy Dispense, which is a contract that governs the exchange of pharmacy dispense data. These elements are crucial in ensuring that health data exchange systems are interoperable and can seamlessly share data, thereby enhancing the efficiency and effectiveness of healthcare delivery.

Example: An example of the application of the Health eDispensation Data Exchange Technical Interoperability Agreement Solutions ABB could be a healthcare network implementing a new electronic prescription system. They would need to adhere to the SCRIPT - ePrescription exchange contract to ensure that their system is compatible with others. Similarly, a pharmacy implementing a new dispensing system would need to comply with the IHE DIS: Pharmacy Dispense contract to ensure interoperability with other systems.

LOST view: TVA-Health eDispensation Enablers [Motivation]

Identifier: http://data.europa.eu/dr8/egovera/HealthEDispensationDataExchangeTechnicalInteroperabilityAgreementSolutionsGrouping

